T18:04:54.675549+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.1","local_name":"bob-cli-ib.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-ib","agent_clan_generation":"20261107124517","bead_id":"bob-cli-ib.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-ib[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Crontabs as code through chezmoi, with first-class agent access[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]One committed cron: block in the chezmoi repo is the single source [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]of truth for every machine's user crontab; chezmoi update -a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]converges each machine's own marked block without touching other [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]lines, and agents can read and write any machine's crontab from any[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]machine through cronctl, a /crontab skill, and a global memory [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]note.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]crontab_as_code.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/crontab_as_code.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-ib[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-ib/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cron data schema, partials, and per-machine rendering[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]render[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]render: add the cron: schema, validating chezmoi partials, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]per-machine managed.crontab and retire.crontab targets, and render tests[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on chezmoi v2.13.1 and the latest release.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Machine-agnostic job runner[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cronrun[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cronrun: add ~/bin/cronrun, which derives the job environment at run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]time, guards overlaps, logs, records status, mails only failures, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]offers a side-effect-free --dry-run.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Local reconciler, hook, and offline cronctl commands[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sync[dim] · [dim][/dim]after render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync: create cronctl with list, render, and check plus the marked-block [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync reconciler, and the run_onchange hook that runs it when this [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine's block changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fleet commands for status, diff, apply, logs, run, and edit[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]remote[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sync, cronrun[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]remote: add SSH-streamed fleet commands so any machine can read live [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state and converge any machine to a pushed revision without a bootstrap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]step.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Crontab skill, memory note, README, and alias cleanup[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]agent-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after remote[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-docs: teach agents the read and write flow through a global [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/crontab skill and reference memory note, document the human flow, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retire legacy cron aliases.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Move athena and Mac jobs into the data and cut over[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after remote, cronrun, agent-docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: move the live athena and Mac jobs into cron: data with an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]atomic cutover, update bob-cli docs, and converge the fleet through a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]post-commit apply.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-ib","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-ib.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e4e41107c84ad98f7c724642d456205b","started_at":"2026-11-07T17:51:11.253855+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.1","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.2","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.3","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.4","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.5","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.6","bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-ib.land"]}
